# the wasm object as a neutral object and back
#
# a wasm object's index spaces become entries: its types first, then each
# space with its imports before its definitions, functions, tables, memories,
# globals and tags, then its data segments. a function's entry names its type
# entry as its signature, an import's entry its module and field, and a
# defined function's or segment's entry its section. every defined function
# is one text section of its body, every data segment one section named,
# aligned and flagged as its segment info states and of the kind its name
# spells, and every custom section the conventions do not consume one debug
# or metadata section. the symbol table's entries are the object's symbols in
# order, a function, global, table or tag symbol defined at its entry, a data
# symbol placed in its segment's section, and a section symbol at its
# section. the relocation records of each reloc section are relocations of
# the function, segment or custom section they fall in, each of the kind its
# type maps to. COMDATs are groups, init functions give their function
# sections a priority, and an exported symbol an export directive. what the
# neutral model has no record for travels in facts keyed by the format: each
# type, each table, memory, global and tag type, each segment's head, each
# element segment, the data count, the start function, the producers and the
# target features, so the module built back holds what the file held.
#
# the module built from an object lays the sections out in the order the
# specification fixes, then the custom sections in object order, then the
# linking section, the reloc sections and the producers and target features.
# a section size and a linking subsection size are padded to five bytes, as
# clang pads them, and every other number takes its shortest form.

